      {
        "id": "model-branching-compare",
        "moduleId": "branching",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "comparison",
        "title": "补充：三个分支语句各退出什么",
        "markdown": "三个语句的区别在于「退出哪一层」：\n\n| 语句 | 退出对象 | 之后发生什么 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `return` | 整个方法 | 把控制权交回调用者，可带回返回值 |\n| `break` | 最近的循环或 switch | 跳到该结构之后继续执行 |\n| `continue` | 当前这一次循环迭代 | 跳过本轮剩余语句，进入下一轮条件判断 |\n\n例如在循环里遇到 `break`，方法并没有结束；遇到 `return` 才会离开方法。判断执行轨迹时先看语句作用在哪一层，再决定后续路径。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "textbook-branching",
            "textbook-branching-ii"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "check-execution-trace",
        "moduleId": "check-and-transfer",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "exercise",
        "title": "练习：预测执行轨迹",
        "markdown": "阅读下面片段，回答两个问题：\n\n```java\nfor (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) {\n    if (i == 3) {\n        continue;\n    }\n    if (i == 6) {\n        break;\n    }\n    System.out.print(i + \" \");\n}\n```\n\n1. 最终输出哪些数字？\n2. 如果把 `continue` 换成 `break`，输出会怎样变化？\n\n请说明每一步依据的是 decision-making、looping 还是 branching 语句。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "textbook-decision-making",
            "textbook-looping",
            "textbook-branching",
            "textbook-branching-ii"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-recap",
        "moduleId": "check-and-transfer",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "summary",
        "title": "小结：先分类，再读轨迹",
        "markdown": "回顾这一节：control flow 语句分成 decision-making、looping 和 branching 三类；`if/else` 选一支执行，`for`/`while` 重复执行，`return`/`break`/`continue` 提前改变路径。阅读代码时先识别语句属于哪一类，再沿着条件与循环状态推演下一步，就能把静态代码还原成实际执行顺序。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "textbook-control-flow-taxonomy",
            "textbook-branching-ii",
            "check-execution-trace"
          ]
        }
      }
